    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nThis is a related issue to the one in #7983 (observed as part of the same set of CI changes), but hopefully easier to solve.\n\nWhen constructing a cache, the cache directory creation can race, because two processes can observe that the cache does not exist, and then both try and make it.\n\nhttps://github.com/cython/cython/blob/7ad0fffd33a44d93e23779757ad5ed37aa0d5e0e/Cython/Build/Cache.py#L96\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nThis should probably work. I think just passing `exist_ok=True` to `os.makedirs` should do the trick\n\n### OS\n\n_No response_\n\n### Python version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Cython version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
